From b448478a854337acce05c47013d7f37d5630193a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:10:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Add toolbar.compact and panel_rows_tab_height settings

Both settings line rows up with the tab bar height.

The pane toolbar is taller than the tab bar because of its vertical
padding, the gap above secondary rows such as the search bar, and its
32px rows. toolbar.compact drops the padding and the gap and sizes the
primary row so that, with the toolbar's bottom border, it matches the
tab bar. The row only has a minimum height, as in stock Zed, so tall
items such as the project search bar grow it instead of overflowing
into the tab bar. The empty breadcrumbs placeholder that multi-file
diffs show takes the row height instead of 32px.

The rows of the buffer and project search bars are 32px whatever the
density, which left a single-row project search 1px taller than the
tab bar. Under toolbar.compact they are as tall as a tab's content and
stack without gaps, so n rows plus the toolbar's border are n times the
content height plus 1px: one row equals the tab bar. A search error,
which stock tucks into the gap between two rows, gets a row of the
same height instead, so it neither overlaps the input nor breaks the
rhythm. The search bar is the same wherever it appears, so the one
above an agent panel terminal is compacted as well, padding included.

Notices that sit below the primary row, such as the multibuffer hint
or a banner, are content-sized in stock Zed and would break that
rhythm. Each gets a row of at least a tab's content height with its
content centred, and the multibuffer hint drops its vertical padding
to fit. A dismissed Python banner leaves the toolbar instead of
leaving an empty row behind.

Rows in the project, git and outline panels are shorter than the tab
bar next to them, so the sticky rows of the project panel never line up
with it. panel_rows_tab_height gives every row in these panels the tab
bar height.

Both settings default to off and leave the stock layout untouched.

Deserialization uses and_then(|t| t.compact).unwrap_or(false) and
panel_rows_tab_height.unwrap_or(false), accompanied by regression unit
tests ensuring safe defaults when configuration keys are omitted.

Share compact row-height calculations through existing dependency
boundaries. Preserve rem-based defaults and each caller's distinction
between an exact height and a minimum height.
